Release Notes AM335x-PD17.2.0
=============================
 
- Linux Kernel v4.9.47
- Linux Kernel v4.9.47-rt37 (PREEMPT_RT) 
- barebox 2017.10.0
- Yocto 2.3.2 (pyro)
- Qt 5.8
 
Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
 
  see machines.txt
 
Build Environment:
------------------
 
  - Ubuntu 16.04 64Bit
 
New Features:
-------------
 
  - Switched to upstream kernel v4.9
  - All machines are available with PREEMPT_RT patches
  - Added 3,5" capacity display
  - Renamed phyboard-regor-am335x-2 to phyboard-regor-r2-am335x-1
  - Added support to store MAC on EEPROM
 
Known Issues:
-------------
 
  - phycore-am335x-som / phycore-r2-am335x-som:
         * Boot tests showed in about 2 of 2000 boots that the SMSC LAN8710 phy could not be found.
           The PHY ID readout is wrong. The generic PHY driver will take over. Ethernet is still functional in this case.
 
  - phycore-am335x/phycore-r2-am335x:
         * rtc1 (AM335x RTC) has high deviation
 
  - CAN tests with 20kbit/s did not run successfully. All other CANopen standard bit rates are working.
    This can be fixed by switching the clock from 25 to 24 Mhz, but new problems with other components can occur.
